{"text": "Vx TOBACCO COMPANY\n\nMEMORANDUM\nTo: R.Caldarella \u2014L. Rhyne T. Staab\nS. Enloe S. Smith G. Telford\nV. Lindsley K. Sparrow L, Weber\nM.Oriowsky A. Spears J. Young\nA. Pasheluk, \u2014_R. Spell 8. Zolot\n\nFROM: \u2014S.L. Evans\nDATE: April 7, 2000\n\nSUBJECT: 2000 WEEKLY VOLUME PERFORMANCE - ACTUAL VS. BUDGET\n\nAttached is a table summarizing Lorillard's actual year-to-date volume performance\nversus budget through April 7, 2000.\n\nSpecific data detailed are as follows:\n\nLorillard Volumes by Brand\n\u2018YTD 2000 - Actual Vs. Budget\nBalance of 2000 - Actual Now Required Vs. Budget\n\nLorillard Dally Averages by Brand\nYTD 2000 - Actual Vs. Budget\nBalance of 2000 - Actual Now Required Vs. Budget\nLatest 4 Weeks\n\nYolume Performance\n\nLorillard's actual year-to-date shipments of 10.606 billion units are below the original\nbudget (10.770 billion units) by -164 milion units or -1.5%. However, by brand, All Other\n(9.0%), Kent (+5.6%), True (+5.0%) and Newport (+1.3%) are above budget.\n\nRally Averages\n\nLorilard's actual year-to-date daily average is 151.5 million units. But for the\nlatest 4-weeks, the average has decreased to 144.9 milion units.\n\nTo achieve our 2000 budget, the average now required for the remainder of\nthe year (185 Shipping Days) is 173.7 million units per day.\n\n98340175",
